  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\nMembers that share a name across kinds (#346, closes #328). A target that gets a method, a property or an event of one name from different interfaces, such as a Current property and a Current() method, got an imposter that failed with CS0102. These members now take apart names on the imposter, like same-kind members already did. The target's own member names are unchanged.\n\nRe-abstracted ref-returning members (#347, closes #325). A ref-returning interface member with a default body that a derived interface re-abstracts left the target without an implementation. The imposter then failed with CS0535 and no diagnostic. Such a member is now handled like an abstract one: IMP011 is reported and no imposter is generated.\n\nGeneric method type parameters named like the method's generated types (#345, closes #339). A method type parameter named like one of the types generated for its method made the imposter fail to compile. Examples are Get\\<GetDelegate>, Get\\<IGetMethodImposterBuilder> and Get\\<GetMethodImposterCollection> (CS0694, CS1503), and Get\\<Builder> or Get\\<Adapter> (CS0102). The method's generated types and nested classes now take other names in that case.",
